To terminate a C program, you can use the `exit()` function. This function ends the program immediately, returning an exit status to the operating system. Here's how to use it:

```c
#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    printf("Hello, World!\n");
    printf("Press Enter to exit...\n");
    getchar(); // Wait for user input
    exit(0);   // Terminate the program
    return 0;
}
